      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MORNING SUN (2) gets the nod after putting away his rivals at Mackay with ease as favourite, and that came after a close third here. Proven at the trip he gets the claimer on to aid with the big weight. Can make it two on the trot. NEXT STOP JUPITER (8) is in red-hot touch and is the obvious danger, though this is her first look at the mile. Expect her to be the one they need to reel in. REMEMBER THE BOYS (5) is building an excellent record and deserves obvious consideration after taking care of his CL2 opposition here last time. Sure to be very competitive. INTREPID LAD (1) was no match for MORNING SUN last time but had beaten him at this track the run prior. Gets weight relief and reunites with Ashley Butler, who is two from two on him. Not dismissing.",
